repository-code: 'https://github.com/benjaminpcollins/miriutils'
abstract: >-
  miriutils is a Python library designed for the processing
  and analysis of JWST/MIRI (Mid-Infrared Instrument) data.
  The package provides a streamlined workflow through the
  following core components:

  - Cutout Production: miricut.py includes the CutoutManager
  class which handles file selection, coordinate matching of
  sources and cutout production in a straightforward way,
  preserving all relevant FITS extensions of the original
  mosaics.

  - RGB Image Visualisation: All tools related to the creation of RGB composite images are stored in vis.py with a fallback on NIRCam/F444W images when multiple MIRI bands are not available

  - Astrometric Calibration: The astrometry_utils.py module
  provides specialised tools for precise coordinate
  alignment and header updates.

  - Photometry & Pipeline Management: Centered around the
  MIRIPipeline class and photometry_tools.py, it automates
  end-to-end photometric analysis and plotting tasks.
keywords:
  - Aperture photometry
  - Photometry
  - JWST/MIRI
  - JWST/NIRCam
